         "6",
         "list",
         "A data structure for storing ordered values. Data are of arbitrary/unfixed size.",
         "List is a Shopping Cart.:\nImagine you’re pushing a shopping cart down the aisle. Each product you drop into it is a piece of information you want to keep. You place the products in one by one and keep track of the exact order they went in—first, second, third, and so on. There’s no strict limit on how many products your cart can hold; it can grow as big as you need. At any time, you can check the items in the order they were placed, remove some, or add new ones, all while maintaining that original sequence.",
         "val_videos/val_6.mp4",
