         "7",
         "Token (in AI/LLMs)",
         "A tokenizer receives raw text. Based on a fixed vocabulary learned from data, it scans the text and breaks it into a sequence of individual, standardized units (words, subwords, or characters). Each unique unit is then mapped to an integer, creating a numerical sequence that is the only format the model can mathematically process.",
         "Think of how a compiler works. It receives your raw source code. The compiler first understands the program's overall meaning. Based on this understanding, it then scans the text and breaks it into a sequence of individual, standardized units. These units are the only format the rest of the compiler can process.",
         "val_videos/val_7.mp4",
