         "8",
         "Boolean logic",
         "A foundational system of algebra using the binary values {true, false} combined with operators like AND, OR, and NOT to evaluate complex logical propositions to a single true or false result.",
         "Think of running commands in a terminal shell, where each command either succeeds or fails. You can chain these commands together. Sometimes, you might want the next command to run only if the previous one succeeded (AND). Other times, you might set it up so a second command runs as a backup, only if the first one fails (OR). The act of running this backup command is what flips the outcome, making the original failed command count as a success for the overall process (NOT).",
         "val_videos/val_8.mp4",
