         "9",
         "Parallel computing",
         "Coordinating multiple processors or cores to work simultaneously on different parts of a problem.",
         "Imagine you're the head chef in a busy restaurant kitchen preparing for a huge banquet. You (the main program) break down the entire banquet (the large problem) into smaller, manageable tasks. You assign one chef (a processor core) to chop vegetables, another to grill the steaks, and a third to prepare the dessert. All the chefs (the cores) work at their stations at the same time on their specific task (a piece of the problem). This simultaneous work allows you to then coordinate the multiple chefs, ensuring the entire banquet is ready much, much faster than if one person had to do it all alone.",
         "val_videos/val_9.mp4",
         "2",
